.TH CLIPNEST-INSTALL-UPDATE 8 "2026" "clipnest" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
clipnest-install-update \- verify and install a downloaded clipnest .deb
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkexec clipnest-install-update
.I sha256-hex
< clipnest.deb
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invoked only via
.BR pkexec (1), gated by the
.B app.clipnest.install-update
polkit action, from Clipnest's Settings update tab. The .deb is read from
standard input into a root-owned directory; its SHA-256 is compared with the
64-character lowercase hex digest argument and its Package field must be
.BR clipnest ,
and its Version must be strictly newer than the installed one
.RB ( "dpkg --compare-versions" " new " gt " installed" ;
if clipnest is not installed yet, any version is accepted).
Only then is it installed with
.BR "apt-get install -y" .
Input larger than 200 MiB is refused. On any mismatch nothing is installed and the exit status is non-zero. This
closes the race in which a same-user process could replace a user-owned file
while the authentication dialog was open.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Installed.
.TP
.B 1
Refused or failed (bad digest, SHA-256 mismatch, wrong package, oversize input, apt-get failure).
.TP
.B 3
The .deb is not newer than the installed version (downgrade or same-version reinstall refused). Nothing is installed.
.PP
.BR pkexec (1)
itself returns 126 (not authorized/dismissed) or 127.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR clipnest (1),
.BR pkexec (1)
